eturn (new_elements, new_punctuation)\n```\n\nThis handles the core requirement cleanly. The docstring explains what each parameter does and what gets returned. I should verify this works with the given example before adding more complexity.\n\nTesting confirms the logic: `[\"Hello\", \"world\"]` becomes `[\"world\", \"Hello\"]` and `[\"\", \"!\"]` becomes `[\"!\", \"\"]`. For edge cases, if lengths differ, reversing both independently preserves their original association—the punctuation index maps to the corresponding element after reversal.",
